<!-- WHAT HAPPENS WHEN YOU REPORT -->
<section class="content-section" id="safety-process">
    <div class="content-wrapper">
        <h2>What Happens When You Report</h2>

        <h3 style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">Reported content is hidden immediately</h3>
        <p>
            Any content reported for safety review is removed from public view right away&mdash;before
            the review is complete. It is not visible to other community members while it is
            under evaluation.
        </p>

        <h3 style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">Brother Aaron reviews it personally</h3>
        <p>
            Every report is reviewed by Brother Aaron. There is no automated system making
            decisions here. Urgent reports are treated as such and addressed without delay.
            Critical safety situations receive a same-hour response during waking hours.
            High-priority abuse and safety concerns receive a personal follow-up within 24 hours.
            All other reports are reviewed within 48 hours.
        </p>

        <h3 style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">Your identity is never disclosed</h3>
        <p>
            <strong>The identity of anyone who makes a report is never disclosed to the person
            or content being reported.</strong> This is a hard policy with no exceptions.
            If content is removed following a report, the person whose content was removed
            is notified only that their submission did not meet community guidelines.
            The existence of a report is never mentioned.
        </p>

        <h3 style="margin-top: 1.5rem;">You receive an acknowledgment</h3>
        <p>
            Every report receives a response confirming it was received. For urgent and
            critical matters, that acknowledgment comes quickly, along with a personal
            follow-up from Brother Aaron.
        </p>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- IMMINENT DANGER & MANDATORY REPORTING -->
<section class="content-section alt" id="safety-mandatory">
    <div class="content-wrapper">
        <h2>Imminent Danger and Child Safety</h2>

        <p>
            If a report indicates imminent danger to any person&mdash;including any content
            involving potential harm to a child&mdash;it is treated as a critical-priority
            matter and escalated immediately.
        </p>
        <p>
            Your communication with this ministry is treated with the highest respect and
            discretion. In cases involving the safety of a child or imminent danger to any
            person, we may be required by law to involve appropriate authorities.
        </p>
        <p>
            If a child you know may be in danger, you can also contact:
        </p>
        <ul style="margin: 0.75rem 0 0.75rem 1.25rem; line-height: 1.9;">
            <li><strong>Childhelp National Child Abuse Hotline:</strong> 1-800-422-4453 (24/7)</li>
            <li><strong>Emergency services:</strong> 911 (US)</li>
        </ul>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- CRISIS RESOURCES -->
<section class="content-section" id="safety-crisis">
    <div class="content-wrapper">
        <h2>Crisis Resources</h2>

        <p>
            If you are struggling right now&mdash;with thoughts of self-harm, a dangerous
            situation, or anything that feels like too much to carry alone&mdash;please reach
            out for help immediately. You do not have to wait for a response from this community.
        </p>

        <ul style="margin: 1rem 0 1rem 1.25rem; line-height: 2.1;">
            <li><strong>Emergency services:</strong> 911 (US)</li>
            <li><strong>988 Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline:</strong> Call or text <strong>988</strong> (US, available 24/7)</li>
            <li><strong>Crisis Text Line:</strong> Text <strong>HOME</strong> to <strong>741741</strong> (US, available 24/7)</li>
            <li><strong>National Domestic Violence Hotline:</strong> 1-800-799-7233 (24/7)</li>
            <li><strong>Childhelp National Child Abuse Hotline:</strong> 1-800-422-4453 (24/7)</li>
        </ul>

        <p>
            You are not alone. Whatever you are carrying, there are people whose entire
            vocation is to be present to you in it.
        </p>
    </div>
</section>

<!-- CLOSING WORD -->
<section class="content-section alt" id="safety-closing">
    <div class="content-wrapper">
        <h2>A Word from Brother Aaron</h2>

        <p>
            The moment this ministry invited people to share sacred experiences publicly,
            it accepted responsibility for their safety in that space. That is not a legal
            statement. It is a pastoral one.
        </p>
        <p>
            If you are here because something happened and you needed a page like this to
            exist, I am glad it does. Please use it. I take every report seriously, and I
            will respond to you personally.
        </p>
        <p>
            If you are not sure whether what you experienced rises to the level of a
            reportable concern&mdash;report it anyway. You are the right person to decide
            that something deserves attention, and I would rather hear from you than not.
        </p>
